{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01VAHQ83hWkkh8H16GB9YJ7Q","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#ifndef CHTRIE\n2\t#define CHTRIE\n3\t\n4\tstruct chtrie_edge {\n5\t\tstruct chtrie_edge *next;\n6\t\tint from, sym, to;\n7\t};\n8\t\n9\ttypedef struct {\n10\t\tstruct chtrie_edge **etab;\n11\t\tint *idxpool, *idxptr, idxmax;\t/* pool of available node indexes */\n12\t\tint maxn, alphsz, ecap;\n13\t} chtrie;\n14\t\n15\t/* Allocate a trie with at most `n` nodes, and the alphabet size `m`.\n16\t *\n17\t * If `n` or `m` is less than 1, they will be regulated to 1.\n18\t *\n19\t * Nodes in the trie are indexed by non-negative integers less than `n`.\n20\t * The root node is indexed by 0.\n21\t * Symbols are non-negative integers less than `m`.\n22\t *\n23\t * Upon success, return a pointer to the trie.\n24\t * Otherwise, return `NULL` and set `errno`.\n25\t */\n26\tchtrie *chtrie_alloc(size_t n, size_t m);\n27\t\n28\t/* Walk from one node to its child.\n29\t *\n30\t * If the child didn't exist and `creat` is non-zero,\n31\t * a new node will be created.\n32\t *\n33\t * Upon the child is found or created, return the index of the child.\n34\t * Otherwise, return -1.\n35\t * If `creat` is non-zero and this routine fails, `errno` will be set.\n36\t */\n37\tint chtrie_walk(chtrie *tr, int from, int sym, int creat);\n38\t\n39\t/* Delete a child node.\n40\t *\n41\t * If the child doesn't exist, the trie shall be left unchanged.\n42\t */\n43\tvoid chtrie_del(chtrie *tr, int from, int sym);\n44\t\n45\t/* free the trie */\n46\tvoid chtrie_free(chtrie *tr);\n47\t\n48\t#endif\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"457aeea8-d623-49b8-a8c8-a9074eea4de4","uuid":"baad4899-d586-467f-8619-8c0138648421","timestamp":"2026-06-06T04:14:08.022Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-31062124/harvest-crust-9XYVnJ/project/c_src/src/chtrie.h","content":"#ifndef CHTRIE\n#define CHTRIE\n\nstruct chtrie_edge {\n\tstruct chtr